course: dictionary
lesson: 15649
title: Thereabouts: close enough
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Thereabouts» is a useful word when you do not know the exact answer. It means near that place, or near that number, amount or time. Think of it as saying "about" or "roughly".
explain: «The bus arrives at nine o'clock or thereabouts.» The bus is not promised at exactly nine. It will come around nine, a few minutes either side. The word "or" shows that nine o'clock is a guess, and thereabouts makes the guess clear.
explain: Look for the clues. «The cake needs about 200 grams of flour, or thereabouts.» Here the amount is close to 200 grams, but not necessarily exact. In maths, you use thereabouts when you give an estimate, not an exact answer.
fact: «Thereabouts» means near that place, or near that number, amount or time.
fact: Use it when you are making a guess or an estimate, such as «a hundred or thereabouts».
fact: A good check is to swap in "about" or "roughly". If the sentence still makes sense, you have understood it.
fact: US English also uses «thereabout», without the final s.
exercise: «The bus arrives at nine o'clock or thereabouts.» What does thereabouts mean here? | *About nine o'clock | Never at all | Exactly nine o'clock | Nine hours later
exercise: Tom says the lake is 5 km away, or thereabouts. What does thereabouts tell us? | *It is about 5 km away, not exactly | It is exactly 5 km away | It is up in the sky | It is 50 km away
exercise: Which word means about the same as thereabouts? | Never | Inside | Exactly | *Roughly
test: «There are a hundred people in the hall, or thereabouts.» Is the number exact? | No, there are none at all | *No, it is an estimate, about a hundred | Yes, exactly one thousand | Yes, exactly a hundred
test: «He lives in Oxford or thereabouts.» What does thereabouts tell you about where he lives? | He lives on the moon | He lives in Oxford itself, for certain | *He lives near Oxford | He lives in a different country
exam: Which sentence uses thereabouts correctly to mean near that number? | The race is thereabouts in my bag. | *The race takes twenty minutes or thereabouts. | Thereabouts the race is blue. | The race takes thereabouts twenty minutes exactly.
